title: Trade Unions
subtitle: The steps of a union dispute: the demands, the line, mediation, a strike and its end.
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && !!Q.polish_union_rules && PolishUnions.agendaCardAvailable(Q) !}
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
// The agenda of a branch or a dispute (technical reference 14.1–14.5; card catalogue 5.10). Each step costs this
// month's action (1 T, 0 R). The character of a protest in a crisis is chosen by its event, not here, and an offer of
// the government is answered in the answer of the Sejm (17.5.1), for no month (14.3). Since Z — 0.57 (item 11 of the
// play notes of 5 X 2026) it is an ordinary card of the Party deck while a dispute is open or has a cause.
PolishUnions.agendaView(Q);
!}

= The trade unions

[+ pl_un_intro +]

What the numbers mean (0–100): reach — how widely the union reaches the workers of the branch; readiness — how ready they are for action; fatigue — it grows during a strike; trust — in PPS; dissent — discontent with the decisions of the PPS leadership. The fund is the union's money, from which a strike pays every month.

[+ pl_un_summary +]

- @industry
- @rail
- @farm_labour
- @easy_discard

